  "question": {
    "text": "<p>At <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math>, the enthalpy of the following processes are given:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>OH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>242</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>436</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mi>&#916;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>0</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>249</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>What would be the value of X&nbsp;for the following reaction? (Nearest integer)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>OH</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8710;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "499",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>242</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>kJmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;....(1)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>OH</mi><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>78</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; ....(2)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>(</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>436</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp; ....(3)<br />Using Hess&#39;s law of constant heat summation, adding equations(1), (2) and (3) and dividing the net result by 2 we get:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>OH</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#160;&#160;</mo><mn>998</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>499</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />Thus&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>499</mn></math></p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
